-- A claim's due, fixed when it is settled: amount times its person's grade's rate then, divided
-- by 100, rounded half up to two decimals. Null while the claim is not settled, or when it was
-- settled with no rate (n/a): such a claim's due stays live, at the current rate.
ALTER TABLE claim ADD COLUMN due DECIMAL(14,2);
-- The sheet's late percent, two decimals: an overdue claim's due gains it for every full 30 days
-- overdue. Null (or no row) is the default, 0.00.
ALTER TABLE sheet_setting ADD COLUMN late_pct DECIMAL(7, 2);
-- The sheet's floor: a claim's live due is at least it. Null (or no row) is the default, 1.00.
ALTER TABLE sheet_setting ADD COLUMN floor DECIMAL(12,2);

